# Repo-root .dockerignore — applies when building from the repo root context
# (e.g. `docker build -f docker/binding-generator.Dockerfile .`).
#
# Goal: keep host build state out of the binding-generator build context so the
# container starts from a clean repo snapshot and provisions vcpkg organically
# inside the image. This mirrors CI/CD parity — every fresh GitHub Actions runner
# inits the vcpkg submodule and runs `vcpkg install` from scratch (binary cache
# accelerates the build but the source tree is always reconstructed).
#
# Note: docker/.dockerignore continues to apply when building from `./docker`
# context (linux-builder workflow). The two files do not conflict.

# Build outputs
**/bin/
**/obj/
.vs/
artifacts/
.cake-host/

# IDE / editor scratch
.idea/
.vscode/
*.user

# Native build state — the entire vcpkg submodule plus host-side install dir.
# The Dockerfile clones vcpkg fresh at the submodule-pinned commit (VCPKG_COMMIT
# build-arg resolved by tools.cs via `git rev-parse HEAD:external/vcpkg`) and
# bakes vcpkg state into image layers via `vcpkg install` at build time.
vcpkg_installed/
external/vcpkg/

# Generated binding preview output — write-only bind-mount target.
artifacts/generated-bindings-preview/

# .git/ — not needed by the binding-generator image. Layer C clones vcpkg
# directly with a pinned commit; Layer F's full repo COPY consumes only the
# working tree.
.git/

# CI workflows aren't needed at container build time.
.github/

# Other repo metadata not needed at build time.
.claude/
*.log
